VERDICT: PASS -- every claim in the guide's IP Directed Broadcast section was
confirmed in the dataplane, including the one that is visible only in the Ethernet
header, with the SAME frames dropped and then forwarded so that nothing rests on
comparing different stimuli.
      default ............................ 10 directed broadcasts delivered to the
                                           DUT, 0 forwarded
      enabled on the INGRESS interface ... still 0/10 forwarded -- the command is
                                           inert there, and `show running-config`
                                           gives no hint
      enabled on the DESTINATION subnet's
      interface .......................... the identical frames 10/10 forwarded
      translated to a link-layer
      broadcast .......................... egress Ethernet destination
                                           ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff while the IP
                                           destination stays 10.38.22.95
      header preserved ................... the IP source and both UDP ports are
                                           unchanged; only the Ethernet
                                           destination changes
      optional standard ACL .............. permitted source 5/5 forwarded, denied
                                           source 0/5, in ONE capture
      the ACL is consulted per packet .... inverting the permit mirrored the
                                           result exactly, with nothing else
                                           changed
      removal ............................ 0/10 forwarded, control still 5/5
      reboot ............................. the interface command, the ACL binding,
                                           the ACL contents AND the link-layer
                                           translation all survived
CAVEAT:  Proven with one ingress subnet, one destination subnet directly connected
         to the DUT, two UDP flows at 5 frames each and a standard numbered ACL.
         The named-ACL and expanded-range forms that `ip directed-broadcast ?`
         offers were read off the CLI but not exercised. No station on the
         destination subnet consumed the flooded frames: the far side is a
         capture, so what is proven is what the DUT emits onto that subnet. The
         case was not run across more than one routed hop, and the DUT was the
         switch directly connected to the destination subnet throughout.

