  Measurement stance: the subject is whether a specific frame is forwarded and
  TRANSLATED TO A LINK-LAYER BROADCAST on egress. That cannot be seen from a ping
  or from `show running-config`; it is visible only in the Ethernet destination of
  the egress frame (STANDING-ORDERS §7). Every leg crafts the frame on eth3 and
  decodes what arrives on eth4, both MACs included, and carries a routed ICMP
  unicast control which arrived 5/5 in all seven counted legs -- so every zero in
  this log is a measurement and not a dead capture.

STEP 0 -- baseline: prove the commands exist, read-only                           done
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: tools/qmark.py, no trailing carriage return, so nothing is executed. The
  driver's self-test ran first: "self-test OK: 'show clock ?' then Ctrl-U then CR
  executed nothing".

awplus(config-if)#ip directed-broadcast  ?
  <1-99>       IP standard access-list number
  <1300-1999>  IP standard access-list number (expanded range)
  WORD         IP standard named access-list
  <cr>
awplus(config)#access-list 1  ?
  deny    Specify packets to reject
  permit  Specify packets to forward
  <cr>

  => STEP 0 done: `ip directed-broadcast` exists in interface configuration mode
     with a bare form and an optional standard access-list argument in three
     flavours (numbered, expanded-range and named), and the standard numbered ACL
     takes `permit` and `deny`. Nothing in this case is UNSUPPORTED, and the
     optional-ACL limb exercised in STEPs 4 and 5 is a real part of the command
     rather than an assumption.

